// @entry SYN-NOTE
// @desc Human note-rendering prior art: a test vector becomes samples by a
// @desc per-sample loop. For each n: compute the oscillator phase, evaluate
// @desc the sine, scale by amplitude and envelope, floor to an integer PCM
// @desc code, clamp (for mixes), and store little-endian:
// @desc byte[2n] = low 8 bits, byte[2n+1] = high 8 bits.
// @desc The three vector shapes:
// @desc   pure tone:  v = floor(32767*a*sin(phase(f,n)))
// @desc   enveloped:  v = floor(32767*a*adsr(n)*sin(phase(f,n)))
// @desc   mix:        v = clamp(floor(32767*a1*sin(phase(f1,n)))
// @desc                          + floor(32767*a2*sin(phase(f2,n))))
// @desc Sample-exactness matters: the same operations in the same order as
// @desc the reference, or the integer codes drift by one.
